     "text": "{\"count\": 5, \"rationale\": \"The target is an OR of vaultRead, dbReplica, shareMount and mailArchive, so all four must be cut. A valid 5-step cut is {jumpHost, appServer, printServer, fileServer, secretsManager}. (1) Blocking jumpHost (or kerberoast) cuts vaultRead's jumpHost path and also domainAdmin. (2) Blocking appServer kills hypervisor and serviceAccount, which are two of dbReplica's three parents. (3) printServer must be blocked itself, because its parent configSecret is reachable directly from the supplychain foothold. Blocking it removes dbReplica's last parent and one of mailArchive's paths. (4) fileServer must be blocked, since its parents apiToken, rdpLogin and dbLogin are all reachable. (5) secretsManager (or rdpLogin or apiToken) must be blocked to cut shareMount and vaultRead's remaining path. Four steps are not enough. The jumpHost/kerberoast block is needed only for vaultRead's jumpHost path. The hypervisor block (appServer, browserStore or monitoringHost) helps nothing beyond dbReplica. That leaves two blocks for printServer, fileServer and secretsManager. Cutting printServer takes either printServer itself or three blocks (configSecret, ssoLogin, apiToken). No single remaining block cuts both fileServer and secretsManager.\"}"
    }
   ],
